{"title":"Shimano Makes a Major Change to their Road Pedals with SPD-SLR: New Cleats, Pedals, Even Shoes","link":"https://bikerumor.com/new-shimano-spd-slr-pedals-shoes-cleat-for-lower-stack-height-and-faster-clip-in/","date":1789628400000,"content":"<p><img src=\"https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/Shimano-DURA-ACE-PD-R9300-SPD-SLR-And-S-PHYRE-SH-header--1536x1025.png\" width=\"1536\" height=\"1025\" alt=\"Shimano DURA ACE PD R9300 SPD SLR And S PHYRE SH header\" /></p>\n<p>Shimano has spent more than two decades changing almost everything around its road pedals without seriously messing with the SPD-SL cleat. That changes with SPD-SLR.</p>\n\n\n\n<p>The new system brings a redesigned road cleat, new Dura-Ace and Ultegra pedals, and two new road shoes built around a lower shoe-to-pedal connection. Shimano says the complete package cuts stack height by 2.3mm, clips in faster, drops cleat weight, and creates a stiffer connection between the rider and bike. <a href=\"https://www.facebook.com/NBCSportsCycling/videos/disaster-for-mathieu-van-der-poel-on-the-arenberg-and-a-failed-bike-swap-with-ja/818624134630078/\"><em>Just don’t try to ride your teammate’s bike with the new SPD-SLR pedals and you have the SPD-SL cleats…ask Mathieu Van Der Pol.</em></a></p>\n\n\n\n<p>The pedals are interesting, but nothing wildly different; same goes for the S-PHYRE shoes, but the cleat is where the story is.</p>\n\n\n\n<figure><a href=\"https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/Shimano-DURA-ACE-PD-R9300-SPD-SLR-And-S-PHYRE-SH-R910-Lifestyle-Shots-16-Eb84a5-scaled.jpg\"><img width=\"2560\" height=\"1707\" src=\"https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/Shimano-DURA-ACE-PD-R9300-SPD-SLR-And-S-PHYRE-SH-R910-Lifestyle-Shots-16-Eb84a5-scaled.jpg\" alt=\"Shimano DURA ACE PD R9300 SPD SLR And S PHYRE SH R910 Lifestyle Shots 16 Eb84a5\" srcset=\"https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/Shimano-DURA-ACE-PD-R9300-SPD-SLR-And-S-PHYRE-SH-R910-Lifestyle-Shots-16-Eb84a5-scaled.jpg 2560w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/Shimano-DURA-ACE-PD-R9300-SPD-SLR-And-S-PHYRE-SH-R910-Lifestyle-Shots-16-Eb84a5-297x198.jpg 297w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/Shimano-DURA-ACE-PD-R9300-SPD-SLR-And-S-PHYRE-SH-R910-Lifestyle-Shots-16-Eb84a5-1536x1024.jpg 1536w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/Shimano-DURA-ACE-PD-R9300-SPD-SLR-And-S-PHYRE-SH-R910-Lifestyle-Shots-16-Eb84a5-120x80.jpg 120w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/Shimano-DURA-ACE-PD-R9300-SPD-SLR-And-S-PHYRE-SH-R910-Lifestyle-Shots-16-Eb84a5-768x512.jpg 768w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/Shimano-DURA-ACE-PD-R9300-SPD-SLR-And-S-PHYRE-SH-R910-Lifestyle-Shots-16-Eb84a5-2048x1365.jpg 2048w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/Shimano-DURA-ACE-PD-R9300-SPD-SLR-And-S-PHYRE-SH-R910-Lifestyle-Shots-16-Eb84a5-800x533.jpg 800w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/Shimano-DURA-ACE-PD-R9300-SPD-SLR-And-S-PHYRE-SH-R910-Lifestyle-Shots-16-Eb84a5-720x480.jpg 720w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/Shimano-DURA-ACE-PD-R9300-SPD-SLR-And-S-PHYRE-SH-R910-Lifestyle-Shots-16-Eb84a5-1350x900.jpg 1350w\" /></a><figcaption><em>(All Photos/Shimano)</em></figcaption></figure>\n\n\n\n<h3>First Change To SPD-SL Since 2003</h3>\n\n\n\n<p>Shimano introduced SPD-SL in 2003. Shimano has updated pedal bodies, bearings, shoes, and even cleat float options. The basic three-bolt cleat-to-pedal interface has remained remarkably familiar. SPD-SLR is the first fundamental rethink of that connection in more than two decades.</p>\n\n\n\n<p>And, thanks to a tragic attempted bike change at 2026 Paris-Roubaix, we already know why compatibility matters.</p>\n\n\n\n<figure><a href=\"https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/Shimano-DURA-ACE-PD-R9300-SPD-SLR-And-S-PHYRE-SH-in-action-scaled.png\"><img width=\"2560\" height=\"2030\" src=\"https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/Shimano-DURA-ACE-PD-R9300-SPD-SLR-And-S-PHYRE-SH-in-action-scaled.png\" alt=\"Shimano DURA ACE PD R9300 SPD SLR And S PHYRE SH in action\" srcset=\"https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/Shimano-DURA-ACE-PD-R9300-SPD-SLR-And-S-PHYRE-SH-in-action-scaled.png 2560w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/Shimano-DURA-ACE-PD-R9300-SPD-SLR-And-S-PHYRE-SH-in-action-297x236.png 297w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/Shimano-DURA-ACE-PD-R9300-SPD-SLR-And-S-PHYRE-SH-in-action-1536x1218.png 1536w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/Shimano-DURA-ACE-PD-R9300-SPD-SLR-And-S-PHYRE-SH-in-action-120x95.png 120w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/Shimano-DURA-ACE-PD-R9300-SPD-SLR-And-S-PHYRE-SH-in-action-768x609.png 768w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/Shimano-DURA-ACE-PD-R9300-SPD-SLR-And-S-PHYRE-SH-in-action-2048x1624.png 2048w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/Shimano-DURA-ACE-PD-R9300-SPD-SLR-And-S-PHYRE-SH-in-action-1135x900.png 1135w\" /></a></figure>\n\n\n\n<h2>SPD-SLR: Same Idea – Different Connection</h2>\n\n\n\n<p>Shimano is treating SPD-SLR as a complete system, not a new pedal with a slightly different body. If 2026 had a tagline for bike innovation, it would be <em>“think of it as a full system”</em>. </p>\n\n\n\n<p>Shimano developed the shoe, cleat, and pedal together, focusing on reducing movement between the three contact points. The biggest number is a 2.3 mm lower stack height, bringing the foot closer to the pedal axle. </p>\n\n\n\n<figure><a href=\"https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/Shimano-DURA-ACE-PD-R9300-SPD-SLR-And-S-PHYRE-SH-R910-Lifestyle-Shots-10-scaled.jpg\"><img width=\"2560\" height=\"1707\" src=\"https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/Shimano-DURA-ACE-PD-R9300-SPD-SLR-And-S-PHYRE-SH-R910-Lifestyle-Shots-10-scaled.jpg\" alt=\"Shimano DURA ACE PD R9300 SPD SLR And S PHYRE SH R910 Lifestyle Shots 10\" srcset=\"https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/Shimano-DURA-ACE-PD-R9300-SPD-SLR-And-S-PHYRE-SH-R910-Lifestyle-Shots-10-scaled.jpg 2560w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/Shimano-DURA-ACE-PD-R9300-SPD-SLR-And-S-PHYRE-SH-R910-Lifestyle-Shots-10-297x198.jpg 297w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/Shimano-DURA-ACE-PD-R9300-SPD-SLR-And-S-PHYRE-SH-R910-Lifestyle-Shots-10-1536x1024.jpg 1536w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/Shimano-DURA-ACE-PD-R9300-SPD-SLR-And-S-PHYRE-SH-R910-Lifestyle-Shots-10-120x80.jpg 120w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/Shimano-DURA-ACE-PD-R9300-SPD-SLR-And-S-PHYRE-SH-R910-Lifestyle-Shots-10-768x512.jpg 768w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/Shimano-DURA-ACE-PD-R9300-SPD-SLR-And-S-PHYRE-SH-R910-Lifestyle-Shots-10-2048x1365.jpg 2048w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/Shimano-DURA-ACE-PD-R9300-SPD-SLR-And-S-PHYRE-SH-R910-Lifestyle-Shots-10-800x533.jpg 800w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/Shimano-DURA-ACE-PD-R9300-SPD-SLR-And-S-PHYRE-SH-R910-Lifestyle-Shots-10-720x480.jpg 720w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/Shimano-DURA-ACE-PD-R9300-SPD-SLR-And-S-PHYRE-SH-R910-Lifestyle-Shots-10-1350x900.jpg 1350w\" /></a></figure>\n\n\n\n<p><strong><em>Why does stack height matter so much?</em></strong> A couple of millimeters doesn’t sound dramatic until you remember this contact point moves thousands of times over a ride. A lower stack can reduce leverage between the foot and pedal axle, give a rounder pedal stroke, and provide a more stable platform under hard efforts.</p>\n\n\n\n<p>The cleat now sits tighter against the pedal. Shimano claims there is zero gap between the two surfaces as part of the new system’s improved stability and power transfer. That also means a better clip-in experience. </p>\n\n\n\n<figure><a href=\"https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/Shimano-Ultegra-PD-R8200-SPR-SLR-Pedal-shoe-interface--scaled.png\"><img width=\"2543\" height=\"2560\" src=\"https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/Shimano-Ultegra-PD-R8200-SPR-SLR-Pedal-shoe-interface-edited-1-scaled.png\" alt=\"Shimano Ultegra PD R8200 SPR SLR Pedal shoe interface\" srcset=\"https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/Shimano-Ultegra-PD-R8200-SPR-SLR-Pedal-shoe-interface-edited-1-scaled.png 2543w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/Shimano-Ultegra-PD-R8200-SPR-SLR-Pedal-shoe-interface-edited-1-297x300.png 297w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/Shimano-Ultegra-PD-R8200-SPR-SLR-Pedal-shoe-interface-edited-1-1536x1546.png 1536w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/Shimano-Ultegra-PD-R8200-SPR-SLR-Pedal-shoe-interface-edited-1-120x120.png 120w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/Shimano-Ultegra-PD-R8200-SPR-SLR-Pedal-shoe-interface-edited-1-768x773.png 768w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/Shimano-Ultegra-PD-R8200-SPR-SLR-Pedal-shoe-interface-edited-1-1526x1536.png 1526w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/Shimano-Ultegra-PD-R8200-SPR-SLR-Pedal-shoe-interface-edited-1-2035x2048.png 2035w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/Shimano-Ultegra-PD-R8200-SPR-SLR-Pedal-shoe-interface-edited-1-894x900.png 894w\" /></a></figure>\n\n\n\n<h3>SPD-SLR = Faster Clip-In</h3>\n\n\n\n<p>Shimano has widened the catch area and reduced the engagement angle from 15.5 degrees on SPD-SL to 10.5 degrees on SPD-SLR. The smaller angle means less pedal rotation is needed before the cleat finds and engages the pedal. </p>\n\n\n\n<p>The redesigned cleats are also considerably lighter. Shimano says SPD-SLR cleats weigh up to 25% less than their SPD-SL equivalents. <strong><em>Example:</em></strong> The SM-SH12 cleat set weighs 71g compared with 55g for the new CL-SL120. But we’ve yet to actually lay hands on the new cleats. </p>\n\n\n\n<p>Sixteen grams will not transform a bike. However, getting lighter while reducing stack and changing the engagement mechanism is a nice bonus.</p>\n\n\n\n<figure>\n<figure><a href=\"https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/Shimano-DURA-ACE-PD-R9300-SPD-SLR-And-S-PHYRE-SH-red-cleat--scaled.png\"><img width=\"1536\" height=\"1536\" src=\"https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/Shimano-DURA-ACE-PD-R9300-SPD-SLR-And-S-PHYRE-SH-red-cleat--1536x1536.png\" alt=\"Shimano DURA ACE PD R9300 SPD SLR And S PHYRE SH red cleat\" srcset=\"https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/Shimano-DURA-ACE-PD-R9300-SPD-SLR-And-S-PHYRE-SH-red-cleat--1536x1536.png 1536w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/Shimano-DURA-ACE-PD-R9300-SPD-SLR-And-S-PHYRE-SH-red-cleat--297x297.png 297w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/Shimano-DURA-ACE-PD-R9300-SPD-SLR-And-S-PHYRE-SH-red-cleat--120x120.png 120w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/Shimano-DURA-ACE-PD-R9300-SPD-SLR-And-S-PHYRE-SH-red-cleat--768x768.png 768w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/Shimano-DURA-ACE-PD-R9300-SPD-SLR-And-S-PHYRE-SH-red-cleat--2048x2048.png 2048w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/Shimano-DURA-ACE-PD-R9300-SPD-SLR-And-S-PHYRE-SH-red-cleat--900x900.png 900w\" /></a></figure>\n\n\n\n<figure><a href=\"https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/Shimano-DURA-ACE-PD-R9300-SPD-SLR-And-S-PHYRE-SH-blue-cleat--scaled.png\"><img width=\"1536\" height=\"1536\" src=\"https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/Shimano-DURA-ACE-PD-R9300-SPD-SLR-And-S-PHYRE-SH-blue-cleat--1536x1536.png\" alt=\"Shimano DURA ACE PD R9300 SPD SLR And S PHYRE SH blue cleat\" srcset=\"https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/Shimano-DURA-ACE-PD-R9300-SPD-SLR-And-S-PHYRE-SH-blue-cleat--1536x1536.png 1536w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/Shimano-DURA-ACE-PD-R9300-SPD-SLR-And-S-PHYRE-SH-blue-cleat--297x297.png 297w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/Shimano-DURA-ACE-PD-R9300-SPD-SLR-And-S-PHYRE-SH-blue-cleat--120x120.png 120w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/Shimano-DURA-ACE-PD-R9300-SPD-SLR-And-S-PHYRE-SH-blue-cleat--768x768.png 768w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/Shimano-DURA-ACE-PD-R9300-SPD-SLR-And-S-PHYRE-SH-blue-cleat--2048x2048.png 2048w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/Shimano-DURA-ACE-PD-R9300-SPD-SLR-And-S-PHYRE-SH-blue-cleat--900x900.png 900w\" /></a></figure>\n\n\n\n<figure><a href=\"https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/Shimano-DURA-ACE-PD-R9300-SPD-SLR-And-S-PHYRE-SH-yellow-cleat--scaled.png\"><img width=\"1536\" height=\"1536\" src=\"https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/Shimano-DURA-ACE-PD-R9300-SPD-SLR-And-S-PHYRE-SH-yellow-cleat--1536x1536.png\" alt=\"Shimano DURA ACE PD R9300 SPD SLR And S PHYRE SH yellow cleat\" srcset=\"https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/Shimano-DURA-ACE-PD-R9300-SPD-SLR-And-S-PHYRE-SH-yellow-cleat--1536x1536.png 1536w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/Shimano-DURA-ACE-PD-R9300-SPD-SLR-And-S-PHYRE-SH-yellow-cleat--297x297.png 297w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/Shimano-DURA-ACE-PD-R9300-SPD-SLR-And-S-PHYRE-SH-yellow-cleat--120x120.png 120w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/Shimano-DURA-ACE-PD-R9300-SPD-SLR-And-S-PHYRE-SH-yellow-cleat--768x768.png 768w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/Shimano-DURA-ACE-PD-R9300-SPD-SLR-And-S-PHYRE-SH-yellow-cleat--2048x2048.png 2048w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/Shimano-DURA-ACE-PD-R9300-SPD-SLR-And-S-PHYRE-SH-yellow-cleat--900x900.png 900w\" /></a></figure>\n</figure>\n\n\n\n<h3>Four SPD-SLR Cleats</h3>\n\n\n\n<p>Shimano is also expanding the road cleat family from the familiar red, blue, and yellow options to four SPD-SLR versions.</p>\n\n\n\n<ul>\n<li>Red (CL-SL100) is the fixed option with zero float.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Yellow (CL-SL110) is the higher-float option, with Shimano showing ±3 degrees of rotational movement.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Blue (CL-SL120) reduces that to ±1 degree for riders who want some movement without much lateral wandering.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Gray (CL-SL130), which is a little different….</li>\n</ul>\n\n\n\n<figure><a href=\"https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/Shimano-DURA-ACE-PD-R9300-SPD-SLR-And-S-PHYRE-SH-grey-cleat-edited.png\"><img width=\"2267\" height=\"2267\" src=\"https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/Shimano-DURA-ACE-PD-R9300-SPD-SLR-And-S-PHYRE-SH-grey-cleat-edited.png\" alt=\"Shimano DURA ACE PD R9300 SPD SLR And S PHYRE SH grey cleat\" srcset=\"https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/Shimano-DURA-ACE-PD-R9300-SPD-SLR-And-S-PHYRE-SH-grey-cleat-edited.png 2267w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/Shimano-DURA-ACE-PD-R9300-SPD-SLR-And-S-PHYRE-SH-grey-cleat-edited-297x297.png 297w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/Shimano-DURA-ACE-PD-R9300-SPD-SLR-And-S-PHYRE-SH-grey-cleat-edited-1536x1536.png 1536w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/Shimano-DURA-ACE-PD-R9300-SPD-SLR-And-S-PHYRE-SH-grey-cleat-edited-120x120.png 120w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/Shimano-DURA-ACE-PD-R9300-SPD-SLR-And-S-PHYRE-SH-grey-cleat-edited-768x768.png 768w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/Shimano-DURA-ACE-PD-R9300-SPD-SLR-And-S-PHYRE-SH-grey-cleat-edited-2048x2048.png 2048w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/Shimano-DURA-ACE-PD-R9300-SPD-SLR-And-S-PHYRE-SH-grey-cleat-edited-900x900.png 900w\" /></a></figure>\n\n\n\n<p>The gray cleat is intended to help riders use SPD-SLR pedals with most non-Shimano three-bolt road shoes. It provides more adjustment range for shoes with fixed cleat mounting positions, but it does not provide the same low-stack or weight benefits as the three core SPD-SLR cleats. Basically, if you want the low stack and low weight, you’re gonna have to get on the Shimano shoes. But let’s move on to the pedals….</p>\n\n\n\n<figure>\n<figure><a href=\"https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/Shimano-DURA-ACE-PD-R9300-SPD-pedal-back.png\"><img width=\"1536\" height=\"1536\" src=\"https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/Shimano-DURA-ACE-PD-R9300-SPD-pedal-back-1536x1536.png\" alt=\"Shimano DURA ACE PD R9300 SPD pedal back\" srcset=\"https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/Shimano-DURA-ACE-PD-R9300-SPD-pedal-back-1536x1536.png 1536w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/Shimano-DURA-ACE-PD-R9300-SPD-pedal-back-297x297.png 297w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/Shimano-DURA-ACE-PD-R9300-SPD-pedal-back-120x120.png 120w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/Shimano-DURA-ACE-PD-R9300-SPD-pedal-back-768x768.png 768w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/Shimano-DURA-ACE-PD-R9300-SPD-pedal-back-2048x2048.png 2048w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/Shimano-DURA-ACE-PD-R9300-SPD-pedal-back-900x900.png 900w\" /></a></figure>\n\n\n\n<figure><a href=\"https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/Shimano-DURA-ACE-PD-R9300-SPD-pedal-side-.png\"><img width=\"1536\" height=\"1536\" src=\"https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/Shimano-DURA-ACE-PD-R9300-SPD-pedal-side--1536x1536.png\" alt=\"Shimano DURA ACE PD R9300 SPD pedal side\" srcset=\"https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/Shimano-DURA-ACE-PD-R9300-SPD-pedal-side--1536x1536.png 1536w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/Shimano-DURA-ACE-PD-R9300-SPD-pedal-side--297x297.png 297w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/Shimano-DURA-ACE-PD-R9300-SPD-pedal-side--120x120.png 120w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/Shimano-DURA-ACE-PD-R9300-SPD-pedal-side--768x768.png 768w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/Shimano-DURA-ACE-PD-R9300-SPD-pedal-side--2048x2048.png 2048w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/Shimano-DURA-ACE-PD-R9300-SPD-pedal-side--900x900.png 900w\" /></a></figure>\n\n\n\n<figure><a href=\"https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/Shimano-DURA-ACE-PD-R9300-SPD-pedal-top-.png\"><img width=\"1536\" height=\"1536\" src=\"https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/Shimano-DURA-ACE-PD-R9300-SPD-pedal-top--1536x1536.png\" alt=\"Shimano DURA ACE PD R9300 SPD pedal top\" srcset=\"https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/Shimano-DURA-ACE-PD-R9300-SPD-pedal-top--1536x1536.png 1536w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/Shimano-DURA-ACE-PD-R9300-SPD-pedal-top--297x297.png 297w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/Shimano-DURA-ACE-PD-R9300-SPD-pedal-top--120x120.png 120w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/Shimano-DURA-ACE-PD-R9300-SPD-pedal-top--768x768.png 768w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/Shimano-DURA-ACE-PD-R9300-SPD-pedal-top--2048x2048.png 2048w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/Shimano-DURA-ACE-PD-R9300-SPD-pedal-top--900x900.png 900w\" /></a></figure>\n</figure>\n\n\n\n<h3>New Dura-Ace PD-R9300 Pedals</h3>\n\n\n\n<p>SPD-SLR makes its top-level debut on the new Dura-Ace PD-R9300.</p>\n\n\n\n<p>Visually, it still looks like a Shimano road pedal. The changes are in the body shape, contact surface, bearings, and the new cleat interface. The pedal uses an injection-molded carbon-composite body with an extra-wide platform and an integrated stainless steel contact plate. Shimano says the plate improves engagement and increases stiffness at the shoe-pedal interface.</p>\n\n\n\n<figure><a href=\"https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/Shimano-DURA-ACE-PD-R9300-SPD-pedal-bottom--e1789569612778.png\"><img width=\"2284\" height=\"1328\" src=\"https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/Shimano-DURA-ACE-PD-R9300-SPD-pedal-bottom--e1789569612778.png\" alt=\"Shimano DURA ACE PD R9300 SPD pedal bottom\" srcset=\"https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/Shimano-DURA-ACE-PD-R9300-SPD-pedal-bottom--e1789569612778.png 2284w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/Shimano-DURA-ACE-PD-R9300-SPD-pedal-bottom--e1789569612778-297x173.png 297w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/Shimano-DURA-ACE-PD-R9300-SPD-pedal-bottom--e1789569612778-1536x893.png 1536w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/Shimano-DURA-ACE-PD-R9300-SPD-pedal-bottom--e1789569612778-120x70.png 120w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/Shimano-DURA-ACE-PD-R9300-SPD-pedal-bottom--e1789569612778-768x447.png 768w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/Shimano-DURA-ACE-PD-R9300-SPD-pedal-bottom--e1789569612778-2048x1191.png 2048w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/Shimano-DURA-ACE-PD-R9300-SPD-pedal-bottom--e1789569612778-1548x900.png 1548w\" /></a></figure>\n\n\n\n<p>The axle runs on wider bearings intended to spread load more evenly. Shimano claims an 11% increase in stiffness compared with the PD-R8200. Shimano now heat-treats the axle and has revised the bearing surfaces. In this new process, Shimano claims 53% less rotational resistance than the PD-R8200.</p>\n\n\n\n<p>Shimano’s goal was to reduce losses through the entire connection from shoe to axle. It sounds pretty convincing, but thats only if you’re getting on the shoes too.</p>\n\n\n\n<figure>\n<figure><a href=\"https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/Shimano-Ultegra-PD-R8200-SPR-SLR-Pedal-back-side-.png\"><img width=\"1536\" height=\"1536\" src=\"https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/Shimano-Ultegra-PD-R8200-SPR-SLR-Pedal-back-side--1536x1536.png\" alt=\"Shimano Ultegra PD R8200 SPR SLR Pedal back side\" srcset=\"https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/Shimano-Ultegra-PD-R8200-SPR-SLR-Pedal-back-side--1536x1536.png 1536w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/Shimano-Ultegra-PD-R8200-SPR-SLR-Pedal-back-side--297x297.png 297w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/Shimano-Ultegra-PD-R8200-SPR-SLR-Pedal-back-side--120x120.png 120w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/Shimano-Ultegra-PD-R8200-SPR-SLR-Pedal-back-side--768x768.png 768w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/Shimano-Ultegra-PD-R8200-SPR-SLR-Pedal-back-side--2048x2048.png 2048w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/Shimano-Ultegra-PD-R8200-SPR-SLR-Pedal-back-side--900x900.png 900w\" /></a></figure>\n\n\n\n<figure><a href=\"https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/Shimano-Ultegra-PD-R8200-SPR-SLR-Pedal-top-.png\"><img width=\"1536\" height=\"1536\" src=\"https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/Shimano-Ultegra-PD-R8200-SPR-SLR-Pedal-top--1536x1536.png\" alt=\"Shimano Ultegra PD R8200 SPR SLR Pedal top\" srcset=\"https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/Shimano-Ultegra-PD-R8200-SPR-SLR-Pedal-top--1536x1536.png 1536w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/Shimano-Ultegra-PD-R8200-SPR-SLR-Pedal-top--297x297.png 297w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/Shimano-Ultegra-PD-R8200-SPR-SLR-Pedal-top--120x120.png 120w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/Shimano-Ultegra-PD-R8200-SPR-SLR-Pedal-top--768x768.png 768w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/Shimano-Ultegra-PD-R8200-SPR-SLR-Pedal-top--2048x2048.png 2048w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/Shimano-Ultegra-PD-R8200-SPR-SLR-Pedal-top--900x900.png 900w\" /></a></figure>\n\n\n\n<figure><a href=\"https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/Shimano-Ultegra-PD-R8200-SPR-SLR-Pedal-bottompng.png\"><img width=\"1536\" height=\"1536\" src=\"https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/Shimano-Ultegra-PD-R8200-SPR-SLR-Pedal-bottompng-1536x1536.png\" alt=\"Shimano Ultegra PD R8200 SPR SLR Pedal bottompng\" srcset=\"https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/Shimano-Ultegra-PD-R8200-SPR-SLR-Pedal-bottompng-1536x1536.png 1536w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/Shimano-Ultegra-PD-R8200-SPR-SLR-Pedal-bottompng-297x297.png 297w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/Shimano-Ultegra-PD-R8200-SPR-SLR-Pedal-bottompng-120x120.png 120w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/Shimano-Ultegra-PD-R8200-SPR-SLR-Pedal-bottompng-768x768.png 768w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/Shimano-Ultegra-PD-R8200-SPR-SLR-Pedal-bottompng-2048x2048.png 2048w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/Shimano-Ultegra-PD-R8200-SPR-SLR-Pedal-bottompng-900x900.png 900w\" /></a></figure>\n</figure>\n\n\n\n<h3>Ultegra Gets SPD-SLR Too</h3>\n\n\n\n<p>The new Ultegra PD-R8200 uses the same SPD-SLR architecture.</p>\n\n\n\n<p>It gets a lightweight resin body, stainless steel contact plate, and the same engagement characteristics as Dura-Ace. Riders will trade some of the top-tier refinement for a slightly lower price point, but with the same stack height as the Dura-Ace setup. </p>\n\n\n\n<figure><a href=\"https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/Shimano-S-PHYRE-SH-RC910-SPR-SLR-Shoe-blue-side--scaled-e1789569708153.png\"><img width=\"2236\" height=\"973\" src=\"https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/Shimano-S-PHYRE-SH-RC910-SPR-SLR-Shoe-blue-side--scaled-e1789569708153.png\" alt=\"Shimano S PHYRE SH RC910 SPR SLR Shoe blue side\" srcset=\"https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/Shimano-S-PHYRE-SH-RC910-SPR-SLR-Shoe-blue-side--scaled-e1789569708153.png 2236w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/Shimano-S-PHYRE-SH-RC910-SPR-SLR-Shoe-blue-side--scaled-e1789569708153-297x129.png 297w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/Shimano-S-PHYRE-SH-RC910-SPR-SLR-Shoe-blue-side--scaled-e1789569708153-1536x668.png 1536w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/Shimano-S-PHYRE-SH-RC910-SPR-SLR-Shoe-blue-side--scaled-e1789569708153-120x52.png 120w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/Shimano-S-PHYRE-SH-RC910-SPR-SLR-Shoe-blue-side--scaled-e1789569708153-768x334.png 768w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/Shimano-S-PHYRE-SH-RC910-SPR-SLR-Shoe-blue-side--scaled-e1789569708153-2048x891.png 2048w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/Shimano-S-PHYRE-SH-RC910-SPR-SLR-Shoe-blue-side--scaled-e1789569708153-1600x696.png 1600w\" /></a></figure>\n\n\n\n<h3>New S-PHYRE RC910</h3>\n\n\n\n<p>Shimano also built a new flagship shoe around the lower SPD-SLR interface, and it’s pretty integral to the whole system.</p>\n\n\n\n<p>The S-PHYRE SH-RC910 gets a new Carbon Hollow Core midsole, carbon-fiber heel cup with Anti-Twist Stabilization, revised surround-wrapping upper, additional ventilation, and DYNALAST 2.0. The SPD-SLR mounting platform should give riders more cleat adjustment range.</p>\n\n\n\n<figure><a href=\"https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/Shimano-S-PHYRE-SH-RC910-SPR-SLR-Shoe.-blue-bottom--scaled-e1789569760133.png\"><img width=\"2270\" height=\"1070\" src=\"https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/Shimano-S-PHYRE-SH-RC910-SPR-SLR-Shoe.-blue-bottom--scaled-e1789569760133.png\" alt=\"Shimano S PHYRE SH RC910 SPR SLR Shoe. blue bottom\" srcset=\"https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/Shimano-S-PHYRE-SH-RC910-SPR-SLR-Shoe.-blue-bottom--scaled-e1789569760133.png 2270w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/Shimano-S-PHYRE-SH-RC910-SPR-SLR-Shoe.-blue-bottom--scaled-e1789569760133-297x140.png 297w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/Shimano-S-PHYRE-SH-RC910-SPR-SLR-Shoe.-blue-bottom--scaled-e1789569760133-1536x724.png 1536w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/Shimano-S-PHYRE-SH-RC910-SPR-SLR-Shoe.-blue-bottom--scaled-e1789569760133-120x57.png 120w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/Shimano-S-PHYRE-SH-RC910-SPR-SLR-Shoe.-blue-bottom--scaled-e1789569760133-768x362.png 768w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/Shimano-S-PHYRE-SH-RC910-SPR-SLR-Shoe.-blue-bottom--scaled-e1789569760133-2048x965.png 2048w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/Shimano-S-PHYRE-SH-RC910-SPR-SLR-Shoe.-blue-bottom--scaled-e1789569760133-1600x754.png 1600w\" /></a></figure>\n\n\n\n<p>Shimano says the Carbon Hollow Core construction aims for maximum pedaling efficiency while keeping weight down. The carbon heel structure is meant to keep the back of the foot from twisting under hard efforts. The previous S-PHYRE used nylon heel retention and felt OK to us, but I wouldn’t mind carbon if it’s comfortable. </p>\n\n\n\n<p>The lower cleat interface is part of the shoe, not something Shimano popped underneath an existing RC903. </p>\n\n\n\n<figure><a href=\"https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/Shimano-S-PHYRE-SH-RC910-SPR-SLR-Shoe-white-bottom-scaled-e1789569870860.png\"><img width=\"2295\" height=\"990\" src=\"https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/Shimano-S-PHYRE-SH-RC910-SPR-SLR-Shoe-white-bottom-scaled-e1789569870860.png\" alt=\"Shimano S PHYRE SH RC910 SPR SLR Shoe white bottom\" srcset=\"https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/Shimano-S-PHYRE-SH-RC910-SPR-SLR-Shoe-white-bottom-scaled-e1789569870860.png 2295w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/Shimano-S-PHYRE-SH-RC910-SPR-SLR-Shoe-white-bottom-scaled-e1789569870860-297x128.png 297w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/Shimano-S-PHYRE-SH-RC910-SPR-SLR-Shoe-white-bottom-scaled-e1789569870860-1536x663.png 1536w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/Shimano-S-PHYRE-SH-RC910-SPR-SLR-Shoe-white-bottom-scaled-e1789569870860-120x52.png 120w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/Shimano-S-PHYRE-SH-RC910-SPR-SLR-Shoe-white-bottom-scaled-e1789569870860-768x331.png 768w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/Shimano-S-PHYRE-SH-RC910-SPR-SLR-Shoe-white-bottom-scaled-e1789569870860-2048x883.png 2048w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/Shimano-S-PHYRE-SH-RC910-SPR-SLR-Shoe-white-bottom-scaled-e1789569870860-1600x690.png 1600w\" /></a></figure>\n\n\n\n<h3>RC810 Brings the Platform Down a Level</h3>\n\n\n\n<p>The new SH-RC810 brings much of the same thinking to the tier below S-PHYRE.</p>\n\n\n\n<p>It uses dual BOA Li2 dials, DYNALAST 2.0, an external heel stabilizer, replaceable heel pads, and a hollow-channel carbon midsole with ventilation and water drainage.</p>\n\n\n\n<p>Most importantly, it gets the new SPD-SLR mounting platform and expanded cleat adjustment.</p>\n\n\n\n<p>That gives Shimano two shoes (at different price points) built around the new interface from launch, while still letting riders with existing Shimano three-bolt road shoes use the new cleats.</p>\n\n\n\n<figure><a href=\"https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/Shimano-DURA-ACE-PD-R9300-SPD-SLR-And-S-PHYRE-SH-action--scaled.jpg\"><img width=\"2560\" height=\"1707\" src=\"https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/Shimano-DURA-ACE-PD-R9300-SPD-SLR-And-S-PHYRE-SH-action--scaled.jpg\" alt=\"Shimano DURA ACE PD R9300 SPD SLR And S PHYRE SH action\" srcset=\"https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/Shimano-DURA-ACE-PD-R9300-SPD-SLR-And-S-PHYRE-SH-action--scaled.jpg 2560w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/Shimano-DURA-ACE-PD-R9300-SPD-SLR-And-S-PHYRE-SH-action--297x198.jpg 297w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/Shimano-DURA-ACE-PD-R9300-SPD-SLR-And-S-PHYRE-SH-action--1536x1024.jpg 1536w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/Shimano-DURA-ACE-PD-R9300-SPD-SLR-And-S-PHYRE-SH-action--120x80.jpg 120w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/Shimano-DURA-ACE-PD-R9300-SPD-SLR-And-S-PHYRE-SH-action--768x512.jpg 768w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/Shimano-DURA-ACE-PD-R9300-SPD-SLR-And-S-PHYRE-SH-action--2048x1365.jpg 2048w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/Shimano-DURA-ACE-PD-R9300-SPD-SLR-And-S-PHYRE-SH-action--800x533.jpg 800w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/Shimano-DURA-ACE-PD-R9300-SPD-SLR-And-S-PHYRE-SH-action--720x480.jpg 720w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/Shimano-DURA-ACE-PD-R9300-SPD-SLR-And-S-PHYRE-SH-action--1350x900.jpg 1350w\" /></a></figure>\n\n\n\n<h3>Where From Here?</h3>\n\n\n\n<p>For a company that rarely changes standards without a reason, SPD-SLR is a notable move. Shimano has decided there were enough gains left between the sole of the shoe and the pedal axle to justify walking away from more than 20 years of road-pedal compatibility.</p>\n\n\n\n<p>After watching Van der Poel discover that fact in the middle of Arenberg, nobody can say Shimano changed it quietly. But we’ll save our comments until we can experience this new system for ourselves. Until then, remember to check the neutral service bikes next year….</p>","author":"Jordan Villella","comments":"https://bikerumor.com/new-shimano-spd-slr-pedals-shoes-cleat-for-lower-stack-height-and-faster-clip-in/#comments","siteTitle":"Bikerumor","siteHash":"49f427af0a926f4232eb837006841d7242e153e3afbb590f32e4b104ea3e2718","entryHash":"6f9db781b94bbee48f9346b66a2c53718edef69cb05fb71ebac4f0d8de7bf2e4","category":"Cycling"}